Z||000002||JohnF||11-18-2001||11:45 AM||||I don't know about your vaccuum leak however, I believe a specfic fix for a code 35 is to replace the IAC (idle air control).  Reason being is that the code 35 is only set when running engine idle speed goes more than 50 rpm above idle when throttle is closed.<P>No guarantees, though, that this fixes the problem, especially if you do have a vaccuum leak.<P>I just had to throw in my little bit!||||reg||12
Z||000003||PBJ||11-18-2001||11:51 AM||||Get a vacuum guage and plug it into the vacuum lines. The main area's of concern that I have found is the metal tubes along the back section of engine area and vacuum resivior (if you have cruise).  ||||reg||1
